"""Market-class specifications (data only). One entry per *market class*; families map onto classes in market_specs.py.

Each spec states what decides the outcome, the distribution to model, key numbers, what must be verified in
rules_primary, point-in-time hazards, required history, and CONCRETE driver inputs with tier (E/C/X).
These are research hypotheses and requirements - not claims of collection or predictive value.
`settle` lists questions to verify against the versioned rules text (m.rules_text), never assumed facts.
"""

def S(outcome, dist, keys, settle, pit, hist, **drivers):
    return dict(outcome=outcome, distribution=dist, key_numbers=keys, settle=settle, pit=pit, history=hist, drivers=drivers)

